  Measured per-step cost, per dataset (seq = mean padded sequence length):

    task   train     ssl step    ft step    
    --------------------------------------------
    CDDB   2508      6.85s seq53 5.82s seq78
    CORA   142714    17.67s seq114 11.98s seq128
    D2     20014     19.41s seq128 13.06s seq128
    D3     8124      19.37s seq128 13.19s seq128
    D4     1376      13.00s seq92 9.72s seq127
    D5     95194     6.17s seq50 5.69s seq76
    D6     193460    4.26s seq33 4.17s seq58
    D7     4686      18.64s seq124 12.93s seq128
    D8     26050     11.51s seq86 9.79s seq128
    D9     7548      13.33s seq95 11.28s seq127

  Projected wall time per config. Lower bound -- excludes
  --bootstrap and --clustering, which add an encode pass each.

    task   (3,50)      (3,10)      (2,5)       (1,3)       (1,1)      
    ------------------------------------------------------------------
    CDDB   7.5h      ! 1.9h      ! 63m         35m         19m        
    CORA   749.4h    ! 116.1h    ! 51.0h     ! 33.4h     ! 1.8h      !
    D2     129.4h    ! 22.5h     ! 10.5h     ! 6.6h      ! 75m        
    D3     54.5h     ! 10.7h     ! 5.3h      ! 3.2h      ! 60m        
    D4     8.3h      ! 2.7h      ! 1.6h      ! 52m         35m        
    D5     266.0h    ! 42.6h     ! 19.1h     ! 12.3h     ! 69m        
    D6     394.1h    ! 62.4h     ! 27.8h     ! 18.1h     ! 88m        
    D7     31.9h     ! 7.1h      ! 3.7h      ! 2.1h      ! 54m        
    D8     127.5h    ! 21.4h     ! 9.8h      ! 6.2h      ! 56m        
    D9     43.7h     ! 8.4h      ! 4.1h      ! 2.5h      ! 43m        

    '!' = over the 1.5h cap. Those become TIMEOUT rows, which is a
    reportable result -- but a dataset that is '!' in EVERY column
    cannot be searched at all under the frozen protocol, and that
    needs raising with the supervisor.

    (3,50) is the authors' published setting.

